  "generated_text": "1. Calculate the volume of each snowball:\n   - Volume of the first snowball with radius 2 inches: $V_1 = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (2)^3 = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi \\cdot 8 = \\frac{32}{3}\\pi$ inches.\n   - Volume of the second snowball with radius 3 inches: $V_2 = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (3)^3 = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi \\cdot 27 = 36\\pi$ inches.\n   - Volume of the third snowball with radius 5 inches: $V_3 = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (5)^3 = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi \\cdot 125 = \\frac{500}{3}\\pi$ inches.\n\n2. Sum the volumes of the three snowballs:\n   - Total volume, $V_{\\text{total}} = V_1 + V_2 + V_3 = \\frac{32}{3}\\pi + 36\\pi + \\frac{500}{3}\\pi = \\boxed{188\\pi}$.",
